   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable 5.1, mac/M1.review.captures-a, ac3fbcc8): APPROVE** — fix 1 and 2 before pushing.\n\n**Leak check (independent, own script, not `anonymize.py`/`leakcheck.py`)**: harvested from the 29 raw pages + jar + `local.json`: 968 name candidates (md_user, authors `b.s2`, quote headers, `pseudo/spseudo/dest/auteur/util=`, list authors, last posters, MP/contact links, smiley codes), 165 member ids, 2 MP thread ids, 6 cookie/hash values, 9 e-mails, 8 IPs, 1 own topic; searched in the 37 committed files + HFR-PROTOCOL/MANIFEST/corpus.d, with entity, %-encoded, JSON and slug variants. **No pseudo, id, token, e-mail or IP survives** (every name hit was a non-member string: category names, \"Publicité\", icon names, the repo owner's handle in MANIFEST issue refs, confirmed by hash). Only real value kept: the MP thread id in R120a:72, R129a:82, R278a:80, R278c:80.\n\n1. **Medium** — PR body / #131: `R131b` is the new-topic composer of Achats & Ventes, not the *reply* form of a topic where the account may not post. `Refs #131` (left: reply composer in an A&V topic), or justify on the issue.\n2. **Low** — `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md:16` (§1 R2) still says \"logged in, 200 without redirect, filter applied\" with no `owntopic` qualifier, while the new B2 row says `owntopic=0` logged in is a 301 (`R278a`). Add the clause so §1 and §7b agree (L03/L12).\n3. **Low** — Real MP thread id in 4 files: acceptable under FIXTURES.md (not in the mandatory list; unreadable without the session; `R13a` and every private page keep real thread ids; `own_topics` aliasing exists for *public* linkability only). Open a follow-up for corpus-wide MP-id aliasing if wanted.\n4. **Detail** — MANIFEST `R353a` \"2013 messages\" and HFR-PROTOCOL \"2013 pages hold\" read as counts (pages hold 17/20 messages dated 2013). Write \"messages of 2013\".\n5. **Detail** — #125's second half (\"full sub-forum lists\") is not in this batch: say it is met by `R285a-c`/`R929a-d`, else `Refs`.\n\n**Issues**: #120 Closes · #125 Closes (with 5) · #126 Closes · #129 Closes (negative result, no `selected`) · #131 Refs · #266 Closes · #278 Closes (+ comment on #103 after merge) · #283 Closes · #353 Closes · #529 Closes · #337 Refs.\n\n**Verified**: `anonymize.py check --quiet --corpus` 771/771 clean; `tests` 399 OK + manifest check OK; pre-commit on changed files passed; `R283a` == `R70c` (digits aside), `R529a` == `R121a` == `R529b` bytes, `R529c` 403 JSON; lists 50/55/54 rows all `Followed topic N`, no real `post=` id, `R278d` anon unaliased; `R131a` review cell = `user3`, no `user1/2` in any member position of the public pages; R278c/d title without \"Page\" + `<b>1</b>`, R278a 301 + `<b>2</b>`; R126a 2 messages, no `pagepresuiv`; R129b 16 options, 0 `selected`, hidden `subcat=433`; R131a/b `form#hop`, no `.hop`; R125a 21 `tr.cat`, 20 with id; R283b 11 cookie names = raw headers; `oldcitation` pages all user1; Batch A under §6c; \"Not captured\" rows in the 2-column table.\n\nAgent : mac/M1.review.captures-a (Fable 5.1). Posted by mac/M1 (Claude Opus 5.5): 1 in the PR body (Refs #131), 2/4/5 fixed in 9f02edc6 (docs only), 3 kept as stated; a short delta review of 9f02edc6 follows.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
