   "body": "**Adversarial review (Fable 5.1, mac/M1.review.1139, 107703ae, test fix) : APPROVE** — head 107703ae\n\nNo findings.\n\n1. **R283a is HFR's stale-session page, not a parser false positive.** `R283a-home-stale-identity-cookies.html` is 1569 bytes, byte-identical to `R70a-home-stale-session.html` except the two `the_style` cache-busters: a lone `.hop` \"Identifiants invalides !\" and `<meta http-equiv=\"Refresh\" content=\"1; url=/unlog.php?config=hfr.inc\" />`. That matches `docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md:794`. Listing it in `noOtherCapture` is the right fix; `StaleSessionNoticeParser.swift` is untouched.\n2. **Positive case uses the served URL.** `StaleSessionNoticeParserTests.swift:16` pairs R283a with `https://forum.hardware.fr/`, the `GET /` of PROTOCOL §R283a.\n3. **The guard still bites.** Sorted order of the expected list is correct, and the equality check remains exact.\n4. **Nothing else changed.** `git diff --stat 9f02edc6 HEAD`: one file, +6/−2.\n\n**Verified**: `swift test --filter StaleSessionNotice` at 107703ae: 5 tests, all green. Probe (throwaway worktree, since removed): a copy of R283a under another name makes `noOtherCapture` fail, so the test still rejects any other recognized page. Diff of both captures, parser source and PROTOCOL §R283a citation. SwiftLint not installed locally; the change is comments, one tuple row and one string literal (lines < 120).\n\nAgent : mac/M1.review.1139 (Fable 5.1). Posted by mac/M1 (Claude Opus 5.5); test-fix commit by Claude Opus 5.5 (mac/M1).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
